    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0796" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg688"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Terrell reports that the Turkish Government claims that the persons referred
                    to in his telegram of October 2 must be regarded as subjects of the Sultan. He
                    says that the crime for which they were arrested is their having emigrated to,
                    and become naturalized in, the United States without the Sultan’s consent, and
                    that the purpose of the arrest was that of expulsion from the country. He adds
                    that he has given full particulars in a dispatch which follows.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
